# Event Ticketing API

A RESTful API built with Node.js, Express, and MongoDB for managing events, bookings, and users with JWT authentication and role-based access control.

---

## Features

### User Features
- User registration and login
- View events
- Filter events by category and date
- Book tickets
- View own bookings

### Admin Features
- Create, update, and delete events
- View all bookings per event (dashboard)
- Manage seat capacity

### Security
- JWT authentication
- Password hashing with bcrypt
- Role-based access control (user/admin)
- Protected routes

### Bonus Features
- QR code generation for bookings
- QR ticket validation endpoint
- Email confirmation using Nodemailer
- Admin dashboard for event analytics

---

## Tech Stack

- Node.js
- Express.js
- MongoDB & Mongoose
- JWT Authentication
- bcryptjs
- Nodemailer
- qrcode
- dotenv

---

## Installation

```bash
git clone <https://github.com/SirAlexanator/REDINGER_INF653-Final-Project>
cd event-ticketing-api
npm install

Setup Steps
Create a .env file in the root directory
Add required environment variables (see below)
Ensure MongoDB Atlas is running and accessible

PORT=10000
MONGO_URI=your_mongodb_connection_string
JWT_SECRET=your_secret_key
EMAIL_USER=your_email@gmail.com
EMAIL_PASS=your_gmail_app_password

How to Run Locally
Development Mode
npm run dev
Production Mode
npm start
Deployed API
https://your-project-name.onrender.com

API Endpoints
Authentication
POST /api/auth/register
POST /api/auth/login

Events
GET /api/events
GET /api/events/:id
GET /api/events?category=categoryName
GET /api/events?date=YYYY-MM-DD
POST /api/events (admin only)
PUT /api/events/:id (admin only)
DELETE /api/events/:id (admin only)

Bookings
POST /api/bookings
GET /api/bookings
GET /api/bookings/:id
GET /api/bookings/validate/:qr

Admin
GET /api/events/admin/dashboard